<p>Alec Burleson has been quietly having one of the best seasons in the Cardinal clubhouse. One hundred and four RBIs from a first baseman with his contact profile is elite-level consistency, and Roupp&#8217;s slider — which he throws upward of 35 percent of the time — could be a pitch Burleson exploits. The Giants have been vulnerable to lefties on the outside corner this month, and Burleson&#8217;s .811 OPS reflects a hitter who doesn&#8217;t chase. If he sees Roupp early, look for him to work the count and hunt for something to pull.</p>
